<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Arduin of Ivrea</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 955–1015</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Arduin of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivrea">Ivrea</a> was margrave of Ivrea in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> who was elected King of Italy by Italian nobles in 1002, after the death of Emperor Otto III. Opposed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> and by the German king Henry II, he held out until 1014, when he abdicated and retired to a monastery. He was the last native king of Italy before the 19th century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/arduin-of-ivrea.jpg" alt="Arduin of Ivrea" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Davide Papalini · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ivrea-duomo-targa_Arduino.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
